// Things carried: resources by weight, gear by the piece, and the kit a person starts with.
// Loaded once by Content; ContentTests checks every name in here resolves.
//
// resources: every Resource has one row. category is its one category (old ResourceCategories);
//   form is Discrete (counted in pieces, each its own weight, moved whole, never split) or Continuous (one
//   amount); a discrete row gives pieceKg [min, max], the weight of any one piece, and every table that yields
//   it (forage, discoveries, locations, loot, felling, butchering, recipes, the starting pack) stays inside it;
//   kcalPerKg and hydrationMlPerKg are what eating a kilo gives (old ConsumptionHandler), 0 if left out;
//   water must state its hydrationMlPerKg, and only food and water give either.
//   scentLevel (food only, and every food): what a kilo carried or left out gives off to an animal's nose,
//   0-1 (Scent). The spec's order, numbers D: raw meat and fish strong, cooked a little less, dried less
//   again, berries and honey low, nuts and roots near nothing.
//   Which resources burn, and how, is fire.json's; which build shelters is shelters.json's.
// gear: the authored design, by kind id (old Gear factory methods). An item carries only its kind and
//   wear. maxDurability is stated on every kind; -1 never wears out. insulation is tenths of a clo over the slot's share of the
//   body (old BaseInsulation). A tent's shelter values are shelters.json's. capabilities is stated on every
//   kind: what carrying it lets someone do to a thing (Capability names, each once; [] for none). An unlit
//   torch gives no Light: a burning one is a fire, not gear.
//   weapon: damage in units of tissue condition (GLOSSARY.md, Damage), its class, how far
//   from the wielder it strikes (reachM), and, if it is made to be thrown, how far, how true and how hard
//   (thrown). Melee damage is the combat tuner's (Tools/Tune), which holds fights to the outcome order spear >
//   axe > knife > stone > staff > hands (reach counts as well as damage); the heavy and stone-tipped spears it
//   does not tune keep their ratio to the wooden spear, the sharp rock to the knife.
// slotCoverage: the fraction of body surface each slot covers (old Inventory.SlotCoverage). Sums to 1.
// startingPack, startingClothes: the old starting kit (GameContext.CreateNewGame). Pack kilos are
//   listed piece by piece: a discrete resource's pieces as listed, a continuous one's summed in order.
